      "updated": 1795508378870,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. POST /api/contact/connect/:userId\n\n Authenticated user can connect to the\n person whose its id it depends on id to \n accept it or not\n\n2. POST /api/contact/approve/:userId \n\n here the userId is of sender \n\n and the one accepting this request would\n be accepterId\n\n without being in contact, no conversation \n can be started and no messages can be \n sent\n\n3. POST /api/contact/reject/:userId\n\n here the userId is of sender\n\n and the receiver who execute this request \n can decline the contact request of the \n sender \n\n once the request is cancelled, the sender \n can't make a repeating request\n\n4. GET /api/contact/\n\n authenticated user will be displayed with \n all the \"approved\" contact they have\n\n5. GET /api/contact/pending\n\n authenticated user will be displayed with all\n the \"pending\" request to be approved or \n rejected\n\n6. GET /api/contact/rejected\n\n authenticated user will be displayed with \n all the \"rejected\" request\n\n7. PATCH /api/contact/approve/:userId\n\n user requesting this api can approve the \n initially rejected contact requeest made by\n userId \n\n ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. POST /api/contact/connect/:userId\n\n Authenticated user can connect to the\n person whose its id it depends on id to \n accept it or not\n\n2. POST /api/contact/approve/:userId \n\n here the userId is of sender \n\n and the one accepting this request would\n be accepterId\n\n without being in contact, no conversation \n can be started and no messages can be \n sent\n\n3. POST /api/contact/reject/:userId\n\n here the userId is of sender\n\n and the receiver who execute this request \n can decline the contact request of the \n sender \n\n once the request is cancelled, the sender \n can't make a repeating request\n\n4. GET /api/contact/\n\n authenticated user will be displayed with \n all the \"approved\" contact they have\n\n5. GET /api/contact/pending\n\n authenticated user will be displayed with all\n the \"pending\" request to be approved or \n rejected\n\n6. GET /api/contact/rejected\n\n authenticated user will be displayed with \n all the \"rejected\" request\n\n7. PATCH /api/contact/approve/:userId\n\n user requesting this api can approve the \n initially rejected contact requeest made by\n userId \n\n ",
